$TA$ is a chord drawn from the point of contact $T$ of the tangent to a circle, centre $O$.
$C$ and $D$ are points on the circle, with $C$ on the same side of $TA$ as the marked angle, and $D$ on the other side.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,2.2);
\coordinate (L) at (-1.2,2.2);
\coordinate (R) at (1.2,2.2);
\draw (O) circle (2.2);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\draw (L) -- (R);
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\coordinate (A) at (2.152,0.457);
\draw (T) -- (A);
\coordinate (C) at (1.414,1.685);
\coordinate (D) at (-1.994,-0.93);
\draw (T) -- (C) -- (A);
\draw (T) -- (D);
\draw (A) -- (D);
\node[right, xshift=6mm] at (C) {$C$};
\node[left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[right] at (A) {$A$};
\pic[draw, "$39^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--T--R};
\pic[draw, "$?$", angle radius=0.5cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=T--C--A};
\pic[draw, "$?$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--D--T};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which angle, $\angle TCA$ or $\angle TDA$, is equal to the marked tangent-chord angle?

