$XY$ is tangent to a circle at $P$. The points $A$, $B$ and $P$ lie on the circle. Given $\angle PBA=39^{\circ}$ and $\angle BPX=74^{\circ}$, find $\angle APB$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\coordinate (P) at (0,-2);
\coordinate (A) at (-168:2);
\coordinate (B) at (58:2);
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\draw (-2.7,-2) node[left] {$Y$} -- (2.7,-2) node[right] {$X$};
\draw (P) -- (A) -- (B) -- cycle;
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

